# give: objects and coins, the refusals, shopkeepers, and Otho the changer. In the temple (3001): Decimus (10, who
# carries 2,500), Quintus (25), Purser (10, with 100 gold and 503 silver), Seer (20, who sees invisible things) and
# Unseen (5, invisible, though Otho sees it and changes its coins). Mobs: Otho the changer (3162), the baker (3001, a
# shopkeeper) and a fido (3062), Decimus's pet, which carries nothing (it's ordered to get leather pants and a box,
# 3033, which counts as no item but weighs 10). Objects: leather pants (3062), a strange amulet (307, no drop), an
# ivory staff (905, invisible) and three corpses (10, 1000 weight each). Otho starts with 3 gold and 340 silver, so
# 480 silver (change: 4 gold) and then 9 gold (855 silver) are more than he has, and he makes up the difference.
# Worn things can't be given: get_obj_carry skips them, so "You must remove it first" never shows.
@connect dec
Decimus
psswrd
@return
@connect quin
Quintus
psswrd
@return
@connect purse
Purser
psswrd
@return
@connect seer
Seer
psswrd
@return
@connect unseen
Unseen
psswrd
@return
@return
@mob 3162 3001
@mob 3001 3001
@as dec
@mob 3062 3001
@charm pet
@obj 3062 3001
@obj 307 3001
@obj 905 3001
@obj 10 3001
@obj 10 3001
@obj 10 3001
give
give pants
give pants quintus
get pants
get amulet
give pants nobody
give sword quintus
give pants baker
give amulet quintus
give pants fido
give pants quintus
@obj 3062 3001
@obj 3033 3001
order fido get pants
@pulse 12
order fido get box
@pulse 12
@state
@as quin
give pants seer
@as seer
get staff
give staff decimus
give staff quintus
@as dec
get corpse
get corpse
@as quin
get corpse
give corpse decimus
@as purse
give 5
give 0 coins decimus
give 5 bananas decimus
give 5 coins
give 5 coins nobody
give 9999 gold decimus
give 9999 silver decimus
give 10 coins decimus
give 2 gold decimus
give 3 coin decimus
give 5 silver otho
give 480 silver otho
give 9 gold otho
@state
drop 20 silver
@as unseen
get coins
give 20 silver otho
@state
